# MyDuid — Cursor Rules

Before any task, read the repository-root `AGENTS.md`. It is the canonical source of product requirements, roadmap, architecture, security, financial invariants, design direction, and workflow.

## Required behavior
- Treat MyDuid as an existing application. Extend working code; do not rebuild, duplicate, or replace existing functionality with mocks.
- Inspect relevant files and Git status before editing. Verify actual implementation instead of inferring from screenshots or filenames.
- Work only within the assigned scope. Do not perform broad refactors or add dependencies without approval.
- Preserve the installed React 19 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind 4 frontend and Laravel 13 + PostgreSQL + Sanctum SPA backend.
- Money is integer Rupiah only. Never use float for money.
- Keep financial data scoped to the authenticated user. Never trust client-supplied user_id.
- Preserve session-cookie/CSRF SPA authentication; do not add browser-stored bearer tokens.
- Transfers are separate from income/expense and atomic.
- Do not edit existing migrations; use new migrations for schema changes.
- AI uses controlled backend financial tools, not unrestricted SQL. Require confirmation before persisting AI-generated changes.
- Reuse existing components, API contracts, services, utilities, design tokens, and tests.
- UI language is Indonesian. Use lucide-react, no emoji in product UI. Maintain accessibility, 44px touch targets, keyboard focus, and prefers-reduced-motion.
- No destructive database actions, secrets exposure, commit, push, or deployment unless explicitly requested.
- Report changed files and only the checks actually executed. Never claim unverified success.

Follow the phased MyDuid redesign roadmap and approved themes in root `AGENTS.md`. Cursor is the primary agent for scoped multi-file UI implementation; do not run concurrent agents on the same files.
